Below is a **complete, copy‑and‑paste‑ready** example that works with **MapLibre GL JS v6** (the current stable version at the time of writing).

* 40 + SVG icons are fetched from your own domain (`https://my‑site.com/icons/…`).  
* Each venue in the GeoJSON source has a `category` property that matches one of those icon file names (e.g. `"cafe"`, `"park"` …).  
* The icons are added **at runtime** with `map.addImage()`.  
* The symbol layer uses the expression `["get","category"]` so the correct icon is chosen for each feature.  
* Collision handling is left at the default (`icon‑allow‑overlap: false`) so icons that would overlap are automatically hidden when you zoom out.  
* A tiny helper (`loadSvgImage`) rasterises the SVG into an `HTMLImageElement` that `addImage` can accept.  
* The code also checks `map.hasImage()` first, so you can safely reload the page or add more icons later without “image already exists” errors.

---

## 1️⃣  HTML skeleton

```html
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <title>MapLibre – 5 000 venues with SVG icons</title>
  <meta name="viewport" content="initial-scale=1, width=device-width">
  <link href="https://unpkg.com/maplibre-gl@6.11.2/dist/maplibre-gl.css" rel="stylesheet"/>
  <style>
    body, html { margin:0; padding:0; height:100%; }
    #map { position:absolute; top:0; bottom:0; width:100%; }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
<div id="map"></div>

<script src="https://unpkg.com/maplibre-gl@6.11.2/dist/maplibre-gl.js"></script>
<script>
/* --------------------------------------------------------------
   CONFIGURATION
   -------------------------------------------------------------- */
const MAPBOX_ACCESS_TOKEN = '';               // not needed for plain MapLibre, keep empty
const MAP_STYLE = 'https://demotiles.maplibre.org/style.json'; // any style you like
const ICON_BASE_URL = 'https://my-site.com/icons/'; // <-- change to your domain
const ICON_NAMES = [
  // list every category name that has a matching SVG file
  'cafe', 'park', 'restaurant', 'library', 'school',
  'hospital', 'bank', 'pharmacy', 'hotel', 'bar',
  // … add the rest (≈ 30 more) …
];
const VENUES_GEOJSON_URL = 'https://my-site.com/data/venues.geojson'; // <-- change

/* --------------------------------------------------------------
   HELPER – load an SVG, rasterise it, and return the Image element
   -------------------------------------------------------------- */
function loadSvgImage(url, width = 24, height = 24) {
  return new Promise((resolve, reject) => {
    const img = new Image(width, height);
    img.crossOrigin = 'anonymous';          // required for cross‑origin SVGs
    img.onload = () => resolve(img);
    img.onerror = e => reject(new Error(`Failed to load SVG ${url}`));
    img.src = url;
  });
}

/* --------------------------------------------------------------
   MAIN – initialise the map, load icons, then add source + layer
   -------------------------------------------------------------- */
(async () => {
  // 1️⃣  Initialise the map
  const map = new maplibregl.Map({
    container: 'map',
    style: MAP_STYLE,
    center: [-122.44, 37.76],   // pick a sensible start location
    zoom: 12,
    hash: true
  });

  // Wait for the style to be ready before we start adding images
  await new Promise(resolve => map.once('styledata', resolve));

  // 2️⃣  Load every SVG icon and register it with the map
  //    (run them in parallel – Promise.all)
  await Promise.all(
    ICON_NAMES.map(async name => {
      const id = name; // the ID we will reference in the style
      if (map.hasImage(id)) return; // already present (e.g. from a sprite)

      const url = `${ICON_BASE_URL}${name}.svg`;
      const img = await loadSvgImage(url, 24, 24); // 24 px square – adjust if you like
      // `addImage` options – we keep the defaults (pixelRatio: 1, sdf: false)
      map.addImage(id, img);
    })
  );

  // 3️⃣  Load the venues GeoJSON (you could also fetch it yourself and call
  //    map.addSource('venues', {type:'geojson', data: geojsonObject}))
  const venuesResponse = await fetch(VENUES_GEOJSON_URL);
  if (!venuesResponse.ok) throw new Error('Failed to fetch venues GeoJSON');
  const venuesGeojson = await venuesResponse.json();

  // 4️⃣  Add the source
  map.addSource('venues', {
    type: 'geojson',
    data: venuesGeojson
  });

  // 5️⃣  Add the symbol layer that draws the icons
  map.addLayer({
    id: 'venue-icons',
    type: 'symbol',
    source: 'venues',
    // The icon name comes from the feature property `category`
    layout: {
      'icon-image': ['get', 'category'],   // e.g. "cafe", "park", …
      'icon-size': 1,                      // scale factor – tweak as needed
      // Default collision handling (icon‑allow‑overlap: false) already
      // hides icons that would overlap.  You can fine‑tune it:
      // 'icon-allow-overlap': false,
      // 'icon-ignore-placement': false,
      // 'icon-optional': true   // hide only the icon, keep text (if any)
    },
    paint: {
      // optional: give the icons a subtle halo so they stand out on busy basemaps
      'icon-halo-color': '#fff',
      'icon-halo-width': 1
    }
  });

  // OPTIONAL: if you ever get a missing‑image warning you can supply a fallback
  // map.setMissingStyleImageResolver(async (id) => {
  //   // try to load the SVG on‑the‑fly, add it, then return the image data
  //   const img = await loadSvgImage(`${ICON_BASE_URL}${id}.svg`);
  //   map.addImage(id, img);
  //   return img;
  // });

  console.log('✅ All icons loaded, venues displayed');
})();
</script>
</body>
</html>
```

---

## How it works, step‑by‑step

| Step | What happens | Why it matters |
|------|--------------|----------------|
| **Map creation** | `new maplibregl.Map({ … })` | Starts the GL canvas and loads the base style. |
| **`styledata` event** | Wait until the style (including any sprite) is parsed. | `addImage` can only be called **after** the style is ready. |
| **Load each SVG** | `loadSvgImage()` creates an `Image` element, rasterising the SVG at the desired pixel size. | `Map.addImage()` expects an `HTMLImageElement` (or `ImageData`, `Canvas`, etc.). |
| **`map.addImage(id, img)`** | Registers the rasterised SVG under the same ID as the category name. | Symbol layers later refer to this ID via `icon-image`. |
| **`map.hasImage(id)` guard** | Prevents “image already exists” errors if the same icon is added twice (e.g. when hot‑reloading). |
| **Add GeoJSON source** | `map.addSource('venues', …)` | Supplies the 5 000 point features. |
| **Add symbol layer** | `icon-image: ['get','category']` picks the right icon per feature. | No need for a separate layer per category – one expression does it all. |
| **Collision handling** | Default `icon-allow-overlap: false` → icons that would overlap are hidden. | Keeps the map readable when zoomed out. |
| **Optional halo** | `icon-halo-color` / `icon-halo-width` improves contrast on busy basemaps. | Purely aesthetic, but often useful. |
| **`setMissingStyleImageResolver` (commented)** | Provides a fallback for any icon that wasn’t pre‑loaded. | Handy for debugging or for truly dynamic categories. |

---

### Tweaking the appearance

| Property | Typical values | Effect |
|----------|----------------|--------|
| `icon-size` | `0.8` – `1.5` | Scale the icons up or down. |
| `icon-allow-overlap` | `false` (default) – hide colliding icons.<br>`true` – draw everything (may look cluttered). |
| `icon-ignore-placement` | `true` – treat the icon as a “decorative” element that never blocks other symbols. |
| `icon-optional` | `true` – hide only the icon when it collides, keep any `text-field`. |
| `icon-halo-color` / `icon-halo-width` | `#fff` / `1` – a thin white outline that improves legibility. |
| `icon-pitch-alignment` / `icon-rotation-alignment` | `"map"` or `"viewport"` – control how icons behave when the map is pitched/rotated. |

---

## What to change for your own project

| Placeholder | What to replace |
|-------------|-----------------|
| `ICON_BASE_URL` | The absolute URL that points to the folder containing **`<category>.svg`** files. |
| `ICON_NAMES` | The list of all category strings you have SVGs for (the file name **without** the `.svg` extension). |
| `VENUES_GEOJSON_URL` | URL (or relative path) to the GeoJSON that contains the 5 000 venue features. |
| `MAP_STYLE` | Any MapLibre style you prefer (OSM Bright, your own custom style, etc.). |
| `center` / `zoom` | Initial view that makes sense for your data. |

---

### Gotchas & troubleshooting

| Symptom | Likely cause | Fix |
|---------|--------------|-----|
| **Console: “Image `<id>` could not be loaded”** | The SVG URL returned 404 or CORS blocked it. | Verify the URL works in a browser, and that the server sends `Access‑Control‑Allow‑Origin: *` (or your site’s origin). |
| **Icons appear as blank squares** | The SVG was loaded but `addImage` was called **before** the style finished loading. | Ensure you wait for `styledata` (or `load`) before calling `addImage`. |
| **Too many icons visible when zoomed out** | `icon-allow-overlap` was set to `true` (or `icon-ignore-placement`). | Remove that line or set it to `false`. |
| **Icons are blurry on high‑DPI screens** | You loaded a 24 px rasterisation but the device pixel ratio is > 1. | Either provide higher‑resolution SVGs (same file, just rasterise at `width*devicePixelRatio`) or set `pixelRatio: window.devicePixelRatio` in the `addImage` options: `map.addImage(id, img, {pixelRatio: window.devicePixelRatio});` |
| **Missing badge on a shield** | The `category` value does not match any loaded icon ID. | Double‑check that every possible `category` appears in `ICON_NAMES` (or add a fallback via `setMissingStyleImageResolver`). |

---

## TL;DR – Minimal version (no optional extras)

```js
// after map has loaded …
await Promise.all(
  ['cafe','park','restaurant',/* … */].map(async id => {
    if (!map.hasImage(id)) {
      const img = await loadSvgImage(`${ICON_BASE_URL}${id}.svg`);
      map.addImage(id, img);
    }
  })
);

map.addSource('venues', {type:'geojson', data: venuesGeojson});
map.addLayer({
  id: 'venue-icons',
  type: 'symbol',
  source: 'venues',
  layout: {
    'icon-image': ['get','category']   // auto‑selects the right icon
    // default collision handling hides overlaps
  }
});
```

That’s all you need to display 5 000 points with 40 different SVG icons, while keeping the map readable at every zoom level. Happy mapping!

Below is a **complete, copy‑and‑paste‑ready** example that works with **MapLibre GL JS v6** (the current stable version at the time of writing).

* 40 + SVG icons are fetched from your own domain (`https://my‑site.com/icons/…`).  
* Each icon is rasterised once with an `Image` element and registered with `map.addImage`.  
* The venues are stored in a GeoJSON source (`venues.geojson`).  
* The symbol layer uses the `category` property to pick the right icon (`icon-image: ['get','category']`).  
* Collision handling is left at the default (`icon‑allow‑overlap: false`) so that, when you are zoomed out, icons that would overlap are automatically hidden.  
* A tiny helper (`loadSvgIcon`) makes the SVG‑to‑Image conversion reusable and safe for CORS.

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <title>MapLibre – 5 000 venues with SVG icons</title>
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
  <!-- MapLibre GL JS v6 -->
  <link href="https://unpkg.com/maplibre-gl@6.11.2/dist/maplibre-gl.css" rel="stylesheet"/>
  <script src="https://unpkg.com/maplibre-gl@6.11.2/dist/maplibre-gl.js"></script>

  <style>
    body, html { margin:0; padding:0; height:100%; }
    #map { position:absolute; top:0; bottom:0; width:100%; }
  </style>
</head>

<body>
<div id="map"></div>

<script>
/* --------------------------------------------------------------
   1️⃣  Initialise the map
   -------------------------------------------------------------- */
const map = new maplibregl.Map({
  container: 'map',
  style: 'https://demotiles.maplibre.org/style.json',   // any style you like
  center: [-122.42, 37.77],   // San Francisco (lon, lat)
  zoom: 12
});

/* --------------------------------------------------------------
   2️⃣  Helper – load an SVG, rasterise it, and return the Image
   -------------------------------------------------------------- */
function loadSvgIcon(url, width = 24, height = 24) {
  return new Promise((resolve, reject) => {
    const img = new Image(width, height);
    // Important for cross‑origin SVGs – otherwise addImage throws
    img.crossOrigin = 'anonymous';
    img.onload = () => resolve(img);
    img.onerror = (e) => reject(new Error(`Failed to load SVG ${url}`));
    img.src = url;
  });
}

/* --------------------------------------------------------------
   3️⃣  Load all SVG icons (once) and register them with the map
   -------------------------------------------------------------- */
async function registerIcons() {
  // -----------------------------------------------------------------
  //  a)  List every category name that appears in your data.
  //      The name must match the value stored in the GeoJSON's
  //      `category` property *exactly* (case‑sensitive).
  // -----------------------------------------------------------------
  const categories = [
    'cafe', 'restaurant', 'park', 'library', 'museum',
    'school', 'hospital', 'pharmacy', 'bank', 'atm',
    'post_office', 'hotel', 'bar', 'nightclub', 'cinema',
    'theatre', 'gallery', 'parking', 'fuel', 'bicycle_rental',
    'bus_stop', 'train_station', 'subway_entrance', 'taxi',
    'toilets', 'bench', 'drinking_water', 'playground',
    'waste_basket', 'information', 'post_box', 'police',
    'fire_station', 'embassy', 'church', 'mosque', 'temple',
    'stadium', 'airport', 'harbor'
  ];

  // -----------------------------------------------------------------
  //  b)  Build an array of promises that load each SVG.
  // -----------------------------------------------------------------
  const loadPromises = categories.map(cat => {
    const url = `https://my-site.com/icons/${cat}.svg`;   // <-- change to your domain
    return loadSvgIcon(url).then(img => ({ id: cat, img }));
  });

  // -----------------------------------------------------------------
  //  c)  Wait for every icon to finish loading.
  // -----------------------------------------------------------------
  const loaded = await Promise.all(loadPromises);

  // -----------------------------------------------------------------
  //  d)  Register each image with the map (once the style is ready).
  // -----------------------------------------------------------------
  loaded.forEach(({ id, img }) => {
    if (!map.hasImage(id)) {
      // `addImage` options are optional – you can add `sdf:true` etc.
      map.addImage(id, img);
    }
  });
}

/* --------------------------------------------------------------
   4️⃣  Add the GeoJSON source and the symbol layer (after the map
       and the icons are ready)
   -------------------------------------------------------------- */
async function addVenueLayer() {
  // 1️⃣  Load the icons first – they must exist before the layer is added
  await registerIcons();

  // 2️⃣  Add the GeoJSON source (replace the URL with your own)
  map.addSource('venues', {
    type: 'geojson',
    data: 'https://my-site.com/data/venues.geojson'   // <-- change to your data URL
  });

  // 3️⃣  Add the symbol layer that draws the icons
  map.addLayer({
    id: 'venue-icons',
    type: 'symbol',
    source: 'venues',
    // The icon name comes from the feature property `category`
    layout: {
      'icon-image': ['get', 'category'],   // <-- matches the IDs we added above
      'icon-size': 1,                      // tweak if you want larger/smaller icons
      // Default is `icon-allow-overlap: false`.  We keep that so that
      // overlapping icons are hidden when you are zoomed out.
      // If you *do* want every icon to be drawn regardless of collisions,
      // set `icon-allow-overlap: true` (or `icon-overlap: "always"`).
      // For this use‑case we keep the default behaviour.
      // 'icon-allow-overlap': false,
      // Optional: give a small halo so icons stay visible on busy basemaps
      'icon-halo-color': '#fff',
      'icon-halo-width': 1
    },
    // Paint properties are optional – you can colour the halo, etc.
    paint: {}
  });
}

/* --------------------------------------------------------------
   5️⃣  Kick everything off once the map style has loaded
   -------------------------------------------------------------- */
map.on('load', () => {
  // If any icon fails to load we still want to see the rest, so we
  // catch errors per‑icon inside `registerIcons`.  Here we just log.
  addVenueLayer().catch(err => console.error('Failed to add venue layer:', err));
});

/* --------------------------------------------------------------
   6️⃣  (Optional)  Graceful fallback for missing icons
   -------------------------------------------------------------- */
map.on('styleimagemissing', e => {
  // This fires for any `icon-image` that the map cannot find.
  // You could supply a generic placeholder here instead of silently
  // dropping the symbol.
  console.warn(`Missing icon "${e.id}" – you may want to add a fallback.`);
  // Example fallback (uncomment if you have a generic “unknown” icon):
  // if (!map.hasImage('unknown')) {
  //   loadSvgIcon('https://my-site.com/icons/unknown.svg')
  //     .then(img => map.addImage('unknown', img));
  // }
  // map.setLayoutProperty('venue-icons', 'icon-image', [
  //   'case',
  //   ['has', e.id],
  //   ['get', 'category'],
  //   'unknown'
  // ]);
});
</script>
</body>
</html>
```

### How it works

| Step | What happens | Why it matters |
|------|--------------|----------------|
| **Map init** | `new maplibregl.Map({ … })` | Loads a base style (any style you like). |
| **`loadSvgIcon`** | Creates an `Image` element, sets `crossOrigin='anonymous'`, waits for `onload`. | `Map.addImage` only accepts raster images (`Image`, `HTMLCanvasElement`, `ImageBitmap`). The helper rasterises the SVG once, then re‑uses the same bitmap for every feature. |
| **`registerIcons`** | Loops over every category, loads the SVG, registers it with `map.addImage`. | Icons must exist **before** the layer that references them is added; otherwise the map will emit `styleimagemissing`. |
| **GeoJSON source** | `map.addSource('venues', …)` | Supplies the 5 000 point features. |
| **Symbol layer** | `icon-image: ['get','category']` | The expression pulls the `category` property from each feature and looks up the image with that ID. |
| **Collision handling** | Default `icon-allow-overlap: false`. | When you are zoomed out, overlapping icons are automatically hidden, preventing a “piled‑up” look. |
| **`styleimagemissing` listener** | Logs any missing icon and (optionally) injects a fallback. | Helpful during development; you can also supply a generic “unknown” icon so nothing disappears. |

### Tweaking the appearance

* **Icon size** – change `'icon-size': 1` to `0.8`, `1.2`, etc.  
* **Halo** – adjust `'icon-halo-color'` and `'icon-halo-width'` to improve contrast on busy basemaps.  
* **Overlap override** – if you ever want *all* icons to be drawn (e.g., for a very sparse zoom level), set `'icon-allow-overlap': true` or `'icon-overlap': 'always'`.  
* **Text labels** – you can add a `text-field` that shows the venue name, and use `'icon-text-fit'` if you ever need shield‑style badges.

That’s it! With the code above you’ll see 5 000 venues, each rendered with its own SVG‑derived icon, and the map will automatically hide icons that would otherwise collide when you zoom out. Happy mapping!
